  "evidence_notes": "James, 35, was diagnosed with severe Crohn's two years ago. He also has medication-induced diabetes and osteoporosis from steroids. He was hospitalized and started on IV steroids, which led to diabetes. He then took high-dose prednisone, followed by azathioprine, which helped minimally. His GI pushed for biologics, and he started Remicade after a four-month insurance appeal. Remicade worked for a year, then he developed antibodies. He switched to Humira, which provides about 60% improvement. Methotrexate was added, and he experienced nausea and hair thinning. He is now on calcium, vitamin D, and bisphosphonates for osteoporosis. If the Humira/methotrexate combo fails, the next step is Stelara or Entyvio. Surgery is a looming possibility."
